-- title:
--   Ramified coefficient ring inside a complete local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number that is prime (as a typeclass fact) with $3 \le q$, and let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring which is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, whose residue field is finite and of characteristic $q$. Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\varepsilon \in A$ be a unit with $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon \cdot q$ in $A$. Let $\iota : A \to R$ be a ring homomorphism which is local (the preimage of the maximal ideal of $R$ is contained in that of $A$). The assertion is the existence of a type $W$ together with a commutative ring structure making it a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ such that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\sigma \varpi$, and a local ring homomorphism $g : W \to R$ such that $\sigma$ followed by $g$ equals $\iota$ and such that for every $r \in R$ there is $w \in W$ with $r - g(w)$ in the maximal ideal of $R$, i.e. $g$ induces a surjection onto the residue field of $R$. The proof visibly discards the hypotheses on $q$, on the residue characteristic, and on $\varepsilon$ and the relation $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon q$, which are retained to record the ramification situation intended in applications.
--
--   This is the coefficient-ring step in the Katz–Mazur style analysis of a supersingular deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ is interposed between the base $A$ and the given complete local ring $R$, with the uniformiser of $A$ remaining a uniformiser in $W$ and with $W$ covering the whole residue field of $R$. It is used in the identification of such a ring with a quotient of a power series ring over a regular local base, through [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.exists_ringEquiv_mvPowerSeries_quotient_drinfeldForm_of_isRegularLocalRing`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.exists_ringEquiv_mvPowerSeries_quotient_drinfeldForm_of_isRegularLocalRing).
